## Answer

During the post-mortem discussion about the feature flag confusion, **Alice mandated the following operational policy**:

**"All internal team members must be explicitly assigned to specific test groups rather than random distribution."**

This policy was stated by Alice on **January 19, 2025 at 11:00 AM** in message M0019:

> "💡 New policy: All internal team members must be explicitly assigned to specific test groups rather than random distribution. This will prevent debugging confusion in future feature rollouts."

### Context

The confusion arose because team members were randomly distributed across the 30% new algorithm and 70% old algorithm test groups. This caused:
- Alice to experience the new search algorithm and report it working well
- Charlie to experience the old algorithm and report consistent (but unchanged) behavior
- The team to spend days debugging what they thought was a bug, when they were actually experiencing two different systems

The policy ensures that in future feature rollouts, internal team members will know which test group they're in, making debugging and verification much more straightforward.

